Author: Aravind <52457571+thyaravind@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Jul 9 11:57:12 2026 +0000

    Fix production-readiness issues across shared packages

    Audit-driven correctness, security, and reliability fixes across the
    shared packages/ (SF-41):

    db:
    - Drizzle SQLite transactions now use explicit BEGIN/COMMIT/ROLLBACK so
      awaited operations actually run inside the transaction (previously the
      sync better-sqlite3 wrapper committed before any await, giving no
      atomicity/rollback). Enables the two previously-skipped tx tests.
    - Prisma and Kysely WHERE builders now honor OR/AND connectors with
      correct left-associative grouping (matching Drizzle) instead of
      flattening everything into AND / relying on SQL precedence, which
      returned wrong rows and could leak across row-level namespaces.
    - Singular update()/delete() now reject an empty where clause across
      drizzle/kysely/memory adapters (previously affected all rows).
    - Memory adapter IDs use crypto.randomUUID() instead of Math.random().

    http:
    - CORS: emit Vary: Origin for reflected origins (cache poisoning) and
      never send `*` together with credentials (reflect a concrete origin).
    - Router: return 405 + Allow header when a path exists under another
      method; add configurable maxBodyBytes with 413 enforcement (DoS).

    auth:
    - Resource-authorization middleware now fails closed when no session is
      present instead of calling next() (fail-open bypass).

    oauth:
    - oauth-router: validate returnTo against request origin + allowlist to
      prevent open redirects.
    - oauth-http: per-request timeout on the default fetcher; ignore
      non-positive expires_in to avoid spurious refresh loops.

    storage:
    - GCS/Azure download streams apply backpressure (pause/resume/pull) to
      avoid unbounded memory buffering on large objects.
    - Validate/clamp presigned URL expiry in the S3-compatible adapter.

    queue/metrics/webhooks:
    - MemoryQueueAdapter optional maxSize with reject policy (unbounded
      growth); metrics emitter swallows sink exceptions; webhook delivery
      rejects non-http(s) URLs (SSRF guard).

