const items = [
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1v0h","Closed as already guarded on the current head. `reconcilePermissionDirectoryAfterSettlement` catches both durable outbox drain failures and direct directory-sync failures, logs them, and returns before `recordMutationSuccess`; a regression already verifies a committed push share remains successful when the immediate outbox read throws. No code change was needed for this stale finding."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1xv5","Fixed in e2b41099. The negative codegen assertion now rejects any `projectId` property declaration via an identifier-and-colon regex, including optional and nullable forms. The full DataFn CLI suite passes (100 tests)."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1xwI","Fixed in e2b41099. The E2EE test provider now accepts its key reference and emits that same value from `encrypt`; the re-encryption test asserts the resulting envelope uses `next-key`. The full client suite passes (641 tests)."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1xwP","Closed by clarifying and enforcing the intended contract in e2b41099: `ifMissing` is the complete atomic creation payload selected instead of `partial`, not a base to merge `partial` over. Memory and IndexedDB already follow that contract; Swift was aligned and conflicting-value parity coverage now proves create-payload precedence. The full client suite passes (641 tests), and the Swift datastore/test targets compile."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1xwX","Fixed in e2b41099. Explicit settlement now stops the owner heartbeat before the first fallible lookup, background deletion stops any same-process heartbeat after a confirmed delete, and failed transaction setup releases every already-prequeued task. Lookup-failure and background-recovery regressions pass in the full server suite (948 passed, 1 skipped)."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1xwb","Fixed in e2b41099. Colon-terminated `idPrefix` values are normalized before boundary matching in both reconcile and clone. Added a polymorphic shared-join regression with `task:`/`project:`/`user:` prefixes; the full server suite passes (948 passed, 1 skipped)."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1xwi","Fixed in e2b41099. The thrown `executeShare` path now deletes the already-created public-link row before settling the directory task and rethrowing. Added a storage-failure regression that verifies no token row remains; the full server suite passes."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1xwr","Fixed in e2b41099. The temporal-falsy validation test now closes its server in a `finally` block. The full server suite passes (948 passed, 1 skipped)."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1xw6","Fixed in e2b41099. Schema indexing and all affected query-loading paths now treat empty `fkField`/`foreignKey` aliases as absent and fall back to the generated FK. The empty-alias query regression and full server suite pass."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1xxH","Resolved in e2b41099 by aligning the runtimes to the documented contract: on a missing record, `ifMissing` is the complete create payload and `partial` applies only to an existing record. Swift now makes that atomic choice, and its parity test uses conflicting values to prove `ifMissing` wins. Memory/IndexedDB already had the intended behavior; client tests pass and the Swift datastore/test targets compile."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1xxO","Fixed in e2b41099. MySQL introspection now carries `CHARACTER_MAXIMUM_LENGTH`; schema diff detects unbounded/changed lengths; all migration generators emit `TEXT -> VARCHAR(64)` before the unique index. Added ordering and rollback coverage. The full shared CLI suite passes (73 tests)."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1xxW","Fixed in e2b41099. Rollback index metadata now classifies only genuine TEXT-family columns as unbounded; bounded CHAR/VARCHAR columns no longer receive an invalid prefix or trigger the unbounded-unique rejection. Regression coverage and all 73 shared CLI tests pass."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_7C","Fixed in e2b41099. MySQL column length is now captured during introspection, compared during schema diff, and included in executable up/down column migrations, so added or changed `maxLength` reaches existing installations. Migration ordering and rollback tests pass."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_7L","Fixed in e2b41099. Pre-commit renewal now uses a recursive timeout scheduled only after the previous update settles, so renewal writes cannot overlap or complete out of order. The existing long-running lease regression plus the full server suite pass."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_7f","Fixed in e2b41099. Existing MySQL TEXT columns with a bounded schema requirement are converted with `MODIFY COLUMN ... VARCHAR(n)` before index creation in raw SQL and Kysely migrations. Added explicit `TEXT -> VARCHAR(64) -> UNIQUE INDEX` ordering coverage; all shared CLI tests pass."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_7k","Fixed in e2b41099. Explicit drains stop the pre-commit heartbeat before `findOne`, so lookup rejection, missing rows, and region-mismatch exits cannot leave the owner lease renewing. A failing-lookup regression verifies no subsequent renewal occurs."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_7p","Fixed in e2b41099. `currentTextColumns` now contains only unbounded TEXT-family types, never CHAR/VARCHAR. A bounded-VARCHAR changed-index rollback regression verifies Kysely generation does not throw or emit lossy prefixes."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_7v","Fixed in e2b41099. Drizzle schema generation and migration diffing now share validated bounded-string semantics; MySQL introspection supplies the existing length and the migration emits the corresponding column alteration. Full shared CLI validation passes."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_70","Fixed in e2b41099. Legacy adapters no longer receive a create-only payload chosen after a racy `getRecord`; they receive only the merge-safe patch. Complete create defaults are reserved for adapters declaring atomic `ifMissing`. The contract/docs and tests were updated, and all 641 client tests pass."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_73","Fixed in e2b41099. If setup fails after earlier unshare tasks were prequeued, every created task is released with `markPermissionDirectorySyncReady`; that stops each heartbeat before its fallible update and makes successful releases immediately eligible for background recovery."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_77","Fixed in e2b41099. The copyable adapter skeleton no longer advertises atomic `ifMissing`. The detailed example and overview now state that the capability may be declared only with a real transaction, mutex, or optimistic-concurrency primitive, and that `ifMissing` is the complete create payload."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_8D","Fixed in e2b41099. A confirmed outbox-task delete now stops any same-process pre-commit heartbeat. Added a background-recovery regression that advances beyond the lease window and verifies no post-delete updates occur."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_8K","Fixed in e2b41099. The bridge already forwarded `options.ifMissing`; the Swift datastore now atomically selects that complete payload on absence instead of merging `partial` over it, matching Memory and IndexedDB. Conflicting-value parity coverage compiles."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_8U","Fixed in e2b41099. MySQL `maxLength` generation now rejects non-integers, non-positive values, and bounds above the conservative utf8mb4-safe per-column limit of 16,383 characters. All SQL/Kysely/Drizzle generators have rejection coverage."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_8X","Fixed in e2b41099. The primary and nested query-loading paths now use truthy FK-alias fallback, so an empty legacy alias resolves to the generated `categoryId`; schema validation uses the same rule. The exact regression and full server suite pass."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_8e","Fixed in e2b41099. The thrown-share catch now deletes the persisted public-link row in a `try/finally`, settles the directory task, and then rethrows. A regression verifies permission-storage failure leaves no `publicLink` row."],
["PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a1_8l","Closed with the contract correction in e2b41099. `partial` must not win for a missing record when `ifMissing` is provided: `ifMissing` is the complete atomic creation payload. The Swift test now uses conflicting `title` values and asserts `Create` wins and patch-only fields are absent, matching JS adapters and the updated docs."]
];
