        "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Avoid replaying writes after their delete succeeded**\n\nWhen a compacted batch's delete succeeds but another mutation causes the overall push to return `ok: false`, this unconditional full-batch retry replays the omitted merge before the already-applied delete. The server then deduplicates the delete from its cached success instead of executing it again, leaving the record resurrected while the client acknowledges the changelog. Fresh evidence in the current retry fix is that replay is triggered by any batch failure rather than checking whether each omitted write's replacing delete appears in `applied`; only replay writes whose corresponding delete actually failed.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
