        "body": "Resending the full original order after a partially successful compacted request can resurrect a deleted record. For `[write(X), delete(X), failingMutation]`, the first request can apply `delete(X)`, then the retry applies the previously omitted write while server idempotency skips executing that delete again; preserve the replacement ordering/acknowledgement so an applied delete cannot be followed by its omitted write.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Prevent compacted retries from replaying writes after applied deletes\n\n## Affected sites\n- `datafn/client/src/sync/engine.ts:1537-1547` — any failed compacted result causes the complete original batch to be replayed.\n- `datafn/server/src/execution/sync/push.ts:1037-1044` — an already-applied mutation ID is acknowledged without executing its operation again.\n- `datafn/client/src/sync/__tests__/engine.test.ts:339-424` — covers a failed replacement delete, but not a successful delete paired with another failed mutation.\n\n## Required outcome\n- A partial result that applied the compacted delete must never permit its earlier omitted write to execute afterward.\n- Add a regression with an original `[write(X), delete(X), failingMutation]` batch where the compacted delete is applied before the unrelated failure.\n````\n\n</details>",
