            "body": "This only walks `requiredIndexes`, so an indexed MySQL column can still be altered while a current-only index, `PRIMARY`, or foreign-key dependency remains active. For example, `VARCHAR` to `TEXT` leaves an undeclared full-width key in place and MySQL rejects the emitted `MODIFY COLUMN`; preserve every dependency or refuse generation when that cannot be proven.\n\n<details><summary>Technical details</summary>\n\n````markdown\n# Preserve all MySQL dependencies around column changes\n\n## Affected sites\n- `packages/cli/src/utils/schema-diff.ts:404` — considers only indexes declared by the desired schema, not every introspected index covering a changed column.\n- `packages/cli/src/utils/generators.ts:364` — drops only `changedIndexes` and `rebuiltIndexes` before emitting the column alteration.\n- `packages/cli/src/utils/introspection.ts:267` — returns no MySQL constraints, so foreign-key dependencies and inbound references cannot be planned.\n\n## Required outcome\n- Every emitted MySQL type or length change must preserve and correctly sequence all dependent current indexes and foreign keys, including current-only and primary indexes, or fail generation before producing a migration that cannot execute.\n\n## Suggested approach\n- Build dependency records from all introspected indexes covering changed columns and introspect both local and inbound foreign keys; add regressions for an undeclared secondary index and an FK-supported index around `VARCHAR` to `TEXT`.\n````\n\n</details>",
            "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/115#discussion_r3824440358",
            "createdAt": "2026-08-20T18:50:51Z"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6a7Hs6",
      "path": "datafn/server/src/execution/mutation/execute.ts",
      "line": 1571,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
