              "login": "chatgpt-codex-connector"
            },
            "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Do not publish a failed nontransactional share**\n\nWhen a nontransactional adapter runs in SPv2 dual-write mode and the legacy mirror fails after the canonical permission row is written (`share.ts` writes canonical before `mirrorGrantToLegacyV1`), `executeMutationCore` returns a failed result but leaves that row behind. This failure branch then drains the share's outbox task, reads the partial canonical row, and publishes it to the permission directory, granting distributed access even though the caller was told the share failed. Failed shares should compensate the attached failed permission record or discard their task rather than reconciling it as committed state.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
